    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0159" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg153"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 80.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commissioner of the United States to China</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-05-06"><hi rendition="#italic">May 6,
                                1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your information in connection with my
                    Nos. 69 and 74, of April 16 and 26, respectively, concerning the handing over to
                    the <pb facs="0160" n="154" xml:id="pg154"/> Chinese plenipotentiaries of the
                    archives of the Tsungli Yamen, I have the honor to inclose herewith copy of
                    certain correspondence, from which it will be seen that the yamen and archives
                    were duly transferred to Prince Ching and Li Hung-chang on the 1st instant.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>




